 "discussion": "The low pressure, off the southern British Columbia coast, will continue southward today and tomorrow. A couple of the early runs this morning, and the overnight data, bring this system across us tomorrow night (late) and Monday with the snow level lowering to around 5500 feet. A second system will move across us later Wednesday and Thursday."
